---
import BaseHead from "../components/BaseHead.astro";
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from "../consts";
import NavBar from "../components/NavBar.astro";
import TerminalPrompt from "../components/TerminalPrompt.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
    </head>
    <body>
        <NavBar />
        <main>
            <TerminalPrompt />
            <h1>About this site</h1>
            <p>
                I started this website as a hobby project to learn about
                front-end development and CSS styling. My experience is mainly
                in back-end development, so I want improve my front-end
                development skills. The idea is to create my own little corner
                of the internet where I can share some thoughts about topics I
                am interested in.
            </p>
            <p>
                I currently have no social media outside of messaging apps,
                because I think social media is bad for me and society in
                general. But I still want to have some internet presence, for
                example when people want to look me up. That is one of the
                reasons why I created this website
            </p>
            <p>
                <b>Update: </b>In October of 2026 I did a large redesign of my
                website. The new design is based on <a
                    href="https://github.com/tcvscheppingen/DARBS"
                >
                    my build of DWM</a
                > and uses some keybinds. You can press <code>?</code> to view keybinds.
            </p>
            <p>
                The redesign was partially assisted by an LLM, especially
                setting up the keybinds. I used to write this website completely
                by hand and just use an LLM as a spelling and grammar checker.
            </p>
            <p>
                While I am really happy with the new design and fun easter eggs,
                it does not feel like I made it myself. To me, using an AI to
                create something cool feels like cheating on a test. Even though
                my site now looks really cool (in my humble opinion), it feels
                less like <i>my</i> corner of the internet. It feels disingenuous
                to pass this off as my own work.
            </p>
            <p>
                That is why I have decided to stop using AI for development
                entirely. I think AI companies are highly unethical and
                generally do more harm than good.
            </p>
        </main>
        <Footer />
    </body>
</html>
